{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Quail: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja35'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 35 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Kulāvakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nests </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>5. Vaṭṭakajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Quail: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Santi pakkhā apatanā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I have wings that do not fly! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>santi pādā avañcanā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I have feet that do not walk! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mātāpitā ca nikkhantā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Mother and father have fled! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>jātaveda paṭikkamā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Jātaveda the fire: go back! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Vaṭṭakajātakaṁ pañcamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
